IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sa-interpretation-time`

-- Part 9 of the Legislation Interpretation Act 2021 (South Australia): penalties and proceedings for offences.
-- Section 54, the standard scales, is held as a table in sa-part9-standard-scales.l4.
-- This module encodes sections 53 and 55 to 59.
-- Section 53(2) compares moments, so this module imports the time module for `Moment`.

§ `Part 9 -- Penalties and proceedings for offences (sections 53 and 55 to 59)`

§§ `53 -- Penalties`

-- src:570 | (1) A penalty set out at the end of a provision of an Act or a legislative instrument indicates that—
-- src:571 | (a) an offence mentioned in the provision is punishable on finding of guilt by a penalty not exceeding the penalty so set out; or
-- src:572 | (b) if an offence is not mentioned in the provision, a contravention of the provision is an offence punishable on finding of guilt by a penalty not exceeding the penalty so set out.
@ref s 53(1)(a) and (b) (src:570-572)
GIVEN `the penalty set out at the end of the provision, if there is one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the penalty proposed on a finding of guilt` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a penalty may be imposed on a finding of guilt` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the penalty set out at the end of the provision, if there is one`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST `the penalty set out` THEN
            IF `the penalty proposed on a finding of guilt` AT MOST `the penalty set out` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:572 | (b) if an offence is not mentioned in the provision, a contravention of the provision is an offence punishable on finding of guilt by a penalty not exceeding the penalty so set out.
@ref s 53(1)(b) (src:572)
GIVEN `a penalty is set out at the end of the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an offence is mentioned in the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 53(1)(b) makes a contravention of the provision an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `a penalty is set out at the end of the provision` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE (IF `an offence is mentioned in the provision` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE)

DECLARE `Change to the penalty for an offence` IS ONE OF
    `the penalty is increased`
    `the penalty is reduced`

-- Section 53(2)(a): an increase applies "only" to offences committed after it takes effect.
-- Section 53(2)(b): a reduction extends to offences committed before it takes effect, if the penalty is imposed after it takes effect.
-- A reduction and an offence committed after it takes effect: the text does not say, so the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:573 | (2) If the penalty for an offence—
-- src:574 | (a) is increased, the increased penalty applies only to offences committed after the increase takes effect; or
-- src:575 | (b) is reduced, the reduced penalty extends to offences committed before the reduction takes effect (if the penalty is being imposed after the reduction takes effect).
@ref s 53(2) (src:573-575)
GIVEN change IS A `Change to the penalty for an offence`
      `the moment the offence was committed` IS A Moment
      `the moment the change takes effect` IS A Moment
      `the moment the penalty is imposed` IS A Moment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the changed penalty applies to the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER change
        WHEN `the penalty is increased` THEN JUST (`committed after the change takes effect`)
        WHEN `the penalty is reduced` THEN
            IF `committed after the change takes effect` THEN NOTHING
            ELSE JUST (`s 4: the position of a moment in seconds` `the moment the penalty is imposed` GREATER THAN `s 4: the position of a moment in seconds` `the moment the change takes effect`)
    WHERE
        `committed after the change takes effect` MEANS
            `s 4: the position of a moment in seconds` `the moment the offence was committed` GREATER THAN `s 4: the position of a moment in seconds` `the moment the change takes effect`

-- src:576 | (3) In this section—
-- src:577 | penalty includes punishment.
@ref s 53(3) (src:576-577)
GIVEN `it is a punishment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`it is a penalty for section 53` MEANS
    IF `it is a punishment` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `55 -- Fines etc to be paid into Treasury`

-- src:610 | If a fine, penalty or forfeiture is imposed or made by, or authorised to be imposed or made under, any Act, the Act will be taken to provide that the fine, penalty or forfeiture, when recovered, must be paid to the Treasurer of the State and form part of the Consolidated Account.
@ref s 55 (src:610)
GIVEN `a fine, penalty or forfeiture is imposed or made by, or authorised to be imposed or made under, an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 55 requires the recovered fine, penalty or forfeiture to be paid to the Treasurer of the State and to form part of the Consolidated Account` MEANS
    IF `a fine, penalty or forfeiture is imposed or made by, or authorised to be imposed or made under, an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `56 -- References to offences`

-- src:612 | A reference in an Act or a legislative instrument to an offence that is punishable by imprisonment for a specified term or more includes a reference to an offence punishable by imprisonment for life or by an indefinite term.
@ref s 56 (src:612)
GIVEN `the offence is punishable by imprisonment for life or by an indefinite term` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a reference to an offence punishable by imprisonment for a specified term or more includes the offence` MEANS
    IF `the offence is punishable by imprisonment for life or by an indefinite term` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `57 -- Who may proceed for recovery of penalties`

-- src:614 | Any person may take proceedings to recover a fine, penalty or forfeiture imposed by, or authorised to be imposed or awarded under, an Act or a legislative instrument, unless the right to take proceedings is vested by the Act or the legislative instrument in a particular officer or person.
@ref s 57 (src:614)
GIVEN `the Act or instrument vests the right to take proceedings in a particular officer or person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is that officer or person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the person may take proceedings to recover a fine, penalty or forfeiture` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Act or instrument vests the right to take proceedings in a particular officer or person` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE (IF `the person is that officer or person` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE)

§§ `58 -- Interpretation of references to summary proceedings, complaints etc`

-- src:616 | (1) If an Act or a legislative instrument provides that proceedings for offences are to be dealt with, or disposed of, summarily or before a special magistrate or 1 or more justices, those offences will be dealt with under the Criminal Procedure Act 1921 as summary offences.
@ref s 58(1) (src:616)
GIVEN `the Act or instrument provides that proceedings for offences are to be dealt with, or disposed of, summarily or before a special magistrate or 1 or more justices` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 58(1) makes those offences be dealt with under the Criminal Procedure Act 1921 as summary offences` MEANS
    IF `the Act or instrument provides that proceedings for offences are to be dealt with, or disposed of, summarily or before a special magistrate or 1 or more justices` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:617 | (2) If an Act or a legislative instrument provides that a pecuniary sum may be recovered summarily or before or on the award of a special magistrate or 1 or more justices, that sum may be recovered on information in proceedings under the Criminal Procedure Act 1921 and an order for payment made in any such proceedings is enforceable as if it were a fine.
@ref s 58(2) (src:617)
GIVEN `the Act or instrument provides that a pecuniary sum may be recovered summarily or before or on the award of a special magistrate or 1 or more justices` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 58(2) makes the sum recoverable on information in proceedings under the Criminal Procedure Act 1921` MEANS
    IF `the Act or instrument provides that a pecuniary sum may be recovered summarily or before or on the award of a special magistrate or 1 or more justices` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:617 | (2) If an Act or a legislative instrument provides that a pecuniary sum may be recovered summarily or before or on the award of a special magistrate or 1 or more justices, that sum may be recovered on information in proceedings under the Criminal Procedure Act 1921 and an order for payment made in any such proceedings is enforceable as if it were a fine.
@ref s 58(2) (src:617)
GIVEN `the Act or instrument provides that a pecuniary sum may be recovered summarily or before or on the award of a special magistrate or 1 or more justices` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 58(2) makes an order for payment enforceable as if it were a fine` MEANS
    IF `the Act or instrument provides that a pecuniary sum may be recovered summarily or before or on the award of a special magistrate or 1 or more justices` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Expression about a complaint` IS ONE OF
    `a complaint (being an instrument charging a person with a summary offence)`
    `a complainant`
    `making a complaint in respect of an offence`
    `something else about a complaint`

DECLARE `What the expression is taken to be a reference to` IS ONE OF
    `an information under the Criminal Procedure Act 1921`
    `an informant under that Act`
    `laying an information under the Criminal Procedure Act 1921 in respect of an offence of the relevant class`

-- src:618 | (3) A reference in an Act or a legislative instrument to a complaint (being an instrument charging a person with a summary offence) will be taken to be a reference to an information under the Criminal Procedure Act 1921 (and a reference to a complainant will be taken to be a reference to an informant under that Act).
-- src:619 | (4) A reference in an Act or a legislative instrument to making a complaint in respect of an offence will be taken to be a reference to laying an information under the Criminal Procedure Act 1921 in respect of an offence of the relevant class.
@ref s 58(3) and (4) (src:618-619)
GIVEN expression IS A `Expression about a complaint`
GIVETH A MAYBE `What the expression is taken to be a reference to`
`the expression in an Act or legislative instrument is taken to be a reference to` MEANS
    CONSIDER expression
        WHEN `a complaint (being an instrument charging a person with a summary offence)` THEN JUST `an information under the Criminal Procedure Act 1921`
        WHEN `a complainant` THEN JUST `an informant under that Act`
        WHEN `making a complaint in respect of an offence` THEN JUST `laying an information under the Criminal Procedure Act 1921 in respect of an offence of the relevant class`
        WHEN `something else about a complaint` THEN NOTHING

-- src:620 | (5) A reference in an Act or a legislative instrument to a complaint (being an instrument charging a person with a summary offence) other than of a kind contemplated by subsection (3) or (4) is to be construed so as to recognise that, following the commencement of the Summary Procedure (Abolition of Complaints) Amendment Act 2016, all offences are to be charged on information.
@ref s 58(5) (src:620)
GIVEN `the reference is to a complaint (being an instrument charging a person with a summary offence) other than of a kind contemplated by subsection (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the reference is to be construed so as to recognise that all offences are to be charged on information` MEANS
    IF `the reference is to a complaint (being an instrument charging a person with a summary offence) other than of a kind contemplated by subsection (3) or (4)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `59 -- Offences punishable under more than 1 law`

-- src:622 | If an act or omission constitutes an offence under 2 or more Acts, or both under an Act or Acts and at common law, the offender will, unless the contrary intention appears, be liable to be prosecuted and punished under either or any of those Acts or at common law, but is not liable to be punished twice for the same offence.
@ref s 59 (src:622)
GIVEN `the act or omission constitutes an offence under 2 or more Acts, or both under an Act or Acts and at common law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the offender is liable to be prosecuted and punished under either or any of those laws` MEANS
    IF `the act or omission constitutes an offence under 2 or more Acts, or both under an Act or Acts and at common law` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`)
    THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:622 | If an act or omission constitutes an offence under 2 or more Acts, or both under an Act or Acts and at common law, the offender will, unless the contrary intention appears, be liable to be prosecuted and punished under either or any of those Acts or at common law, but is not liable to be punished twice for the same offence.
@ref s 59 (src:622)
`the offender is liable to be punished twice for the same offence` MEANS JUST FALSE

§§ `Tests`

#ASSERT `a penalty may be imposed on a finding of guilt` (JUST 5000) 5000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a penalty may be imposed on a finding of guilt` (JUST 5000) 4999 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a penalty may be imposed on a finding of guilt` (JUST 5000) 5001 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a penalty may be imposed on a finding of guilt` NOTHING 100 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `section 53(1)(b) makes a contravention of the provision an offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 53(1)(b) makes a contravention of the provision an offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `section 53(1)(b) makes a contravention of the provision an offence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 53(2)(a): an increase takes effect at the beginning of 1 July 2026 (s 28).
#ASSERT `the changed penalty applies to the offence` `the penalty is increased` (Moment OF (Date 2 7 2026), 100) (`s 4: the beginning of a day` (Date 1 7 2026)) (Moment OF (Date 3 7 2026), 0) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the changed penalty applies to the offence` `the penalty is increased` (Moment OF (Date 30 6 2026), 86399) (`s 4: the beginning of a day` (Date 1 7 2026)) (Moment OF (Date 3 7 2026), 0) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 53(2)(b): a reduction reaches an earlier offence only when the penalty is imposed after it takes effect.
#ASSERT `the changed penalty applies to the offence` `the penalty is reduced` (Moment OF (Date 30 6 2026), 86399) (`s 4: the beginning of a day` (Date 1 7 2026)) (Moment OF (Date 3 7 2026), 0) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the changed penalty applies to the offence` `the penalty is reduced` (Moment OF (Date 30 6 2026), 86399) (`s 4: the beginning of a day` (Date 1 7 2026)) (Moment OF (Date 30 6 2026), 50000) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the changed penalty applies to the offence` `the penalty is reduced` (Moment OF (Date 2 7 2026), 100) (`s 4: the beginning of a day` (Date 1 7 2026)) (Moment OF (Date 3 7 2026), 0) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `it is a penalty for section 53` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it is a penalty for section 53` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `section 55 requires the recovered fine, penalty or forfeiture to be paid to the Treasurer of the State and to form part of the Consolidated Account` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 55 requires the recovered fine, penalty or forfeiture to be paid to the Treasurer of the State and to form part of the Consolidated Account` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a reference to an offence punishable by imprisonment for a specified term or more includes the offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to an offence punishable by imprisonment for a specified term or more includes the offence` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the person may take proceedings to recover a fine, penalty or forfeiture` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the person may take proceedings to recover a fine, penalty or forfeiture` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the person may take proceedings to recover a fine, penalty or forfeiture` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `section 58(1) makes those offences be dealt with under the Criminal Procedure Act 1921 as summary offences` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 58(1) makes those offences be dealt with under the Criminal Procedure Act 1921 as summary offences` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `section 58(2) makes the sum recoverable on information in proceedings under the Criminal Procedure Act 1921` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 58(2) makes the sum recoverable on information in proceedings under the Criminal Procedure Act 1921` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `section 58(2) makes an order for payment enforceable as if it were a fine` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 58(2) makes an order for payment enforceable as if it were a fine` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the expression in an Act or legislative instrument is taken to be a reference to` `a complaint (being an instrument charging a person with a summary offence)` EQUALS JUST `an information under the Criminal Procedure Act 1921`
#ASSERT `the expression in an Act or legislative instrument is taken to be a reference to` `a complainant` EQUALS JUST `an informant under that Act`
#ASSERT `the expression in an Act or legislative instrument is taken to be a reference to` `making a complaint in respect of an offence` EQUALS JUST `laying an information under the Criminal Procedure Act 1921 in respect of an offence of the relevant class`
#ASSERT `the expression in an Act or legislative instrument is taken to be a reference to` `something else about a complaint` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the reference is to be construed so as to recognise that all offences are to be charged on information` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the reference is to be construed so as to recognise that all offences are to be charged on information` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the offender is liable to be prosecuted and punished under either or any of those laws` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the offender is liable to be prosecuted and punished under either or any of those laws` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the offender is liable to be prosecuted and punished under either or any of those laws` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the offender is liable to be punished twice for the same offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE
